# Changelog & versioning (HARD)

`CHANGELOG.md` is the release memory. Be **specific and strict** - vague “misc” lines are a fail.

## Version policy

- Source of truth for the app version: root `package.json` `"version"`.
- SemVer **patch** only for routine cycles: each completed **cycle** bumps `x.y.Z` by **+0.0.1** (e.g. `0.1.0` → `0.1.1`).
- Do **not** invent minor/major bumps unless the human explicitly asks.
- Keep `package.json` version in lockstep with the newest dated section in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## What is a cycle

A **cycle** ends when a Feature issue closes **or** a Direct-track task batch is done and ready to leave on `development` (same moment as commit + push - see [git-branch](git-branch.mdc)).

One cycle → one patch bump → one dated changelog section. Do not batch multiple finished Features into one version unless the human asked for a single ship.

## On every cycle close (mandatory)

1. Read current `package.json` version; compute `next = patch + 1`.
2. Update root `package.json` `"version"` to `next`.
3. In `CHANGELOG.md`:
   - Ensure work for this cycle is listed under concrete `### Added` / `### Changed` / `### Fixed` / `### Removed` (Keep a Changelog).
   - Promote that work into a new top section (below the title blurb):

```markdown
## [<next>] - YYYY-MM-DD

_Finished: YYYY-MM-DD_

### Added
- **DY-nn / short title** - specific user-visible or technical outcome; Linear/GitHub link when applicable.

### Changed
- …

### Fixed
- …
```

   - Use the **actual finish date** (today in the user/session context, ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`).
   - `_Finished: …_` must match the section date (cycle finish day).
4. Leave `## [Unreleased]` empty (or omit until new work starts). Never leave finished cycle notes only under Unreleased.
5. Entries must be **specific**: issue id, what shipped, surfaces touched (Go / `web/` / docs), and refs. No “various fixes” / “updates”.

## During a cycle (before close)

- Draft bullets under `## [Unreleased]` as work lands (still specific).
- On close, move them into `## [version] - date` and bump `package.json`.

## Required vs optional

| Work | CHANGELOG |
|--|-|
| Feature S+ / user-facing micro-S | **Required** - versioned section on cycle close |
| Direct user-facing fix / polish | **Required** |
| Internal-only harness/docs with no product impact | Optional note under `### Changed` if useful; still bump if you close a cycle that commits product code |

## Anti-patterns

- Shipping a cycle with no dated section / no version bump
- Bumping version without matching `CHANGELOG.md` section
- Dates missing or “sometime this week”
- Duplicate Unreleased + versioned copies of the same bullets
